WEBVTT

NOTE week09-clip3-compounding
NOTE Narration read by an AI-generated voice.
NOTE The clip has its own caption along the bottom of the frame, so these cues
NOTE are placed near the top to keep the two from overlapping.

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.877 line:2 align:center
Every step of an agent is a chance
to fail. It can pick the wrong tool,

2
00:00:04.877 --> 00:00:08.695 line:2 align:center
pass the wrong patient
number, misread a result,

3
00:00:08.695 --> 00:00:11.122 line:2 align:center
or repeat the same call again and again.

4
00:00:11.122 --> 00:00:16.350 line:2 align:center
In ReAct, most failures were
reasoning errors like these.

5
00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:22.472 line:2 align:center
Suppose each step succeeds 95% of the
time, and steps fail independently.

6
00:00:22.472 --> 00:00:27.475 line:2 align:center
Then a task of n steps succeeds
with 0.95 to the power n:

7
00:00:27.475 --> 00:00:30.191 line:2 align:center
0.77 for 5 steps,

8
00:00:30.191 --> 00:00:35.683 line:2 align:center
0.6 for 10, and only 0.36 for 20.

9
00:00:35.883 --> 00:00:42.719 line:2 align:center
Raise each step to 99%, and 10
steps succeed 90% of the time,

10
00:00:42.719 --> 00:00:49.617 line:2 align:center
20 steps 82%. A small gain per step
makes a large difference for long tasks.

11
00:00:49.817 --> 00:00:54.732 line:2 align:center
Mitigations start with the tools.
The agent checks its own results,

12
00:00:54.732 --> 00:00:59.940 line:2 align:center
for example by re-reading the lab
table, and a mismatch stops the task.

13
00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:04.342 line:2 align:center
It gets only read-only tools,
such as get labs and get meds,

14
00:01:04.342 --> 00:01:08.483 line:2 align:center
never one that places
orders or sends messages.

15
00:01:08.683 --> 00:01:14.135 line:2 align:center
Any action that changes care, such as
an order or a message to a patient,

16
00:01:14.135 --> 00:01:20.712 line:2 align:center
stops at a checkpoint. The agent proposes
it, here a repeat potassium and an ECG,

17
00:01:20.712 --> 00:01:25.617 line:2 align:center
and a clinician approves or
rejects it before anything happens.

18
00:01:25.817 --> 00:01:29.801 line:2 align:center
To sum up: retrieval
grounds answers in sources,

19
00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:34.399 line:2 align:center
tools let the model act on real
data through text it writes,

20
00:01:34.399 --> 00:01:40.490 line:2 align:center
and every added step is another chance to
fail. So check results, limit the tools,

21
00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:43.113 line:2 align:center
and ask a clinician.
